  m_Name: Scene05_FAQ_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene05_FAQ_1
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Good eye, detective. Free electrons in a metal are always jiggling about
    because of heat. They dart in every direction, so on average they go nowhere.
    The voltage doesn't start them moving, it gives all of them a steady drift in
    one direction.
